 "recommendation": "SUB unchanged. No candidate (outcome O3). The registered d_path (E = -0.97 Ah at CK7) is not identifiable (LOO width 0.59 Ah) and is explained by a month-specific Ah-chain lambda, not by the pack's tops; the lambda-free voltage check P2 gives -0.28 Ah from cell 3 alone, and a same-cycle lambda (exploratory) gives no trend (-0.11..+0.04 Ah). Do not use SUB + d_path or SUB + d_top.",
 "for_round_15": [
  "any Ah-chain term must use a lambda from the same checkup cycle (lambda steps up to 0.8e-3, about 0.3 Ah per block, between cycles); round 12's Term3 with the pooled 25 C lambda has the same exposure",
  "register a same-cycle lambda rule (45 C segment of the same cycle; 25 C transfer error -0.03/+0.18 Ah per block) before re-estimating d_path; anchors 1 and 7 have no same-cycle 45 C segment",
  "the pack-native path drift is then at most a few tenths of an Ah at CK7; combined with round 13's tail bound [0, +0.41] Ah the open variable stays the checkup's CV termination and charge rate"
 ],
